{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CexEmPYfgLxpHcWVh9eYB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Implementation Complete ✅\n\nI've successfully implemented the shipment confirm endpoint (`POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm`) with the following changes:\n\n### Changes Made:\n\n1. **ApiError.kt** — Added `SHIPMENT_ALREADY_CANCELLED` error code for the 409 conflict scenario\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt** — Added the `confirm` endpoint that:\n   - Returns **404** (SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND) for non-existent shipments\n   - Returns **409** (SHIPMENT_ALREADY_CANCELLED) when confirming cancelled shipments\n   - Returns **200** with unchanged shipment when already confirmed (idempotent for retries)\n   - Transitions from CREATED → CONFIRMED and persists the change\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — Added 4 comprehensive tests covering:\n   - Confirming a CREATED shipment to CONFIRMED\n   - Idempotency (confirming already CONFIRMED succeeds without change)\n   - Rejection of CANCELLED shipments (409)\n   - Rejection of non-existent shipments (404)\n\n### Test Results:\n\n✅ **All 17 tests pass** (9 shipment tests including the 4 new ones)\n✅ **No build failures**\n✅ **No new dependencies added**\n✅ **Only shipment feature files modified**\n\nThe implementation strictly follows the existing Kotlin + Spring Boot architecture and integrates seamlessly with the error handling patterns already in place."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":199,"cache_read_input_tokens":38674,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":199},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f1d5480a-ae3a-4da1-b53e-e887a2bd2c10","uuid":"e84a53c4-56c0-4000-a701-bfb4ace83c8c","timestamp